# Mutation repair evidence — NEW-CANDIDATE-PORTS W0 (inkling2_loop)

Review of PR #3586 raised two findings. A fresh implementer added hermetic
tests and re-applied the reviewer's mutations at head 288065cb8 to prove each
new test detects the defect. All mutations were applied to byte-for-byte
backups of the two production files; after EVERY mutation the file was copied
back and `sha256sum` matched the original and `git status --porcelain` showed
only the test file modified.

Production files (unchanged at end):
  src/vllm/entrypoints/model_loader.cpp
    sha256 25f4e9078c071a6f4c19bff871231cd934b767745efa057e7ff0
  src/vllm/model_executor/models/inkling2_loop_gguf_config.cpp
    sha256 9627ddb611ccc0980b9c8ccc0b6e9ae18c3eb4363d07bac05f4f9182312147bc

Build + run recipe (each mutation, CPU-only build dir already configured):
  cmake --build /tmp/opencode/vllm-inkling2-build --target test_inkling2_loop_gguf -j4
  /tmp/opencode/vllm-inkling2-build/tests/test_inkling2_loop_gguf

Baseline before any mutation: 11 test cases, 72 assertions, all pass.

## Finding 1 — dead-wiring test gap (production call sites)

New production-path case:
  tests/vllm/models/test_inkling2_loop_gguf.cpp:229
  "inkling2_loop: FromModelDir reaches the loader row and refuses"
It builds a minimal VALID inkling2_loop GGUF in memory (gguf_test::GgufModelBuilder,
no mount), calls LoadedEngine::FromModelDir on the .gguf file, and asserts the
thrown message contains "NEW-CANDIDATE-PORTS" and "forward boundary".

  M1  delete the kGgufArchArms[] row
      ({vllm::kInkling2LoopGgufArch, &vllm::Inkling2LoopHfConfigFromGguf},)
      -> RED: 11 cases / 10 passed / 1 failed; 72 assertions / 70 passed / 2 failed
      -> failing case "FromModelDir reaches the loader row and refuses"
      -> both CHECK(NW-CANDIDATE-PORTS) and CHECK(forward boundary) is NOT correct
      (the dispatch falls through to the generic "architecture not supported" text.)

  M2  delete the `if (IsInkling2LoopGguf(gguf)) { throw ... }` block at ~:2923
      -> RED: 11 / 10 passed / 1 failed; 72 / 70 passed / 2 failed
      -> same failing case and same two substring checks
      (the load continues to ModelRegistry::Resolve and refuses without the row text.)

  M3  delete BOTH (the reviewer's exact mutation)
      -> RED: 11 / 10 passed / 1 failed; 72 / 70 passed / 2 failed
      -> same failing case and same two substring checks

Before this case existed, all three mutations left the focused gate GREEN at
7/7 and 67/67. After it, each turns the focused gate red.

## Finding 2 — loop_config validation not mutation-proven

New hermetic cases (all feed a synthetic GGUF built in memory, no mount; exactly
one field is overridden from the valid default):

  tests/vllm/models/test_inkling2_loop_gguf.cpp:247
    "inkling2_loop: loop core layers outside the block count are refused"
  tests/vllm/models/test_inkling2_loop_gguf.cpp:258
    "inkling2_loop: gate_rank 0 is refused"
  tests/vllm/models/test_inkling2_loop_gguf.cpp:268
    "inkling2_loop: a single fixed-loop pass is refused"

  M4  `if (gate_rank < 1)` -> `if (false)`
      -> RED: 11 / 10 passed / 1 failed; 72 / 71 passed / 1 failed
      -> "gate_rank 0 is refused": CHECK_THROWS_WITH did NOT throw at all

  M5  core-range check -> always-false condition
      (`if (core_start > core_end && core_start < core_end)`; the direct
       `if (false)` form was rejected by -Werror=unused-value because it left
       the old boolean expression as a no-effect statement)
      -> RED: 11 / 10 passed / 1 failed; 72 / 71 passed / 1 failed
      -> "loop core layers outside the block count are refused": did NOT throw

  M6  `if (!is_varloop && num_passes < 2)` -> `if (false)`
      -> RED: 11 / 10 passed / 1 failed; 72 / 71 passed / 1 failed
      -> "a single fixed-loop pass is refused": did NOT throw

Before these cases, the reviewer's M4 left the focused gate GREEN at 7/7 and
67/67. After them, each of M4/M5/M6 turns the focused gate red.

